---
layout: layouts/base.njk
listingPages: true
disclosure: true
pagination:
  data: listingsManifest.listings
  size: 1
  alias: home
permalink: "/homes/{{ home.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ home.address_label }}"
---
{# Real home page. Identity (address label) is manifest data; every fact
   renders at request time from Ezzie's listing_public_read via
   listings.js — facts never live in this repo. #}
<div class="wrap page" data-listing-detail data-listing-id="{{ home.listing_id }}" data-slug="{{ home.slug }}">
  <h1>{{ home.address_label }}</h1>
  {# Broker disclosure (Missouri Real Estate Commission advertising
     rule 20 CSR 2250-8.070): Jen holds an interest in every home here
     and they are not listed by a brokerage entity — the rule's own
     phrase stands prominently with the listing facts. #}
  <p class="owner-broker-line">By owner-broker</p>
  <p data-detail-status>Loading this home's details…</p>
  <p class="past-rental-banner" data-detail-past hidden>Past Rental — this home is rented and not available.</p>
  <p class="coming-soon-banner" data-detail-soon hidden>Coming Soon — this home is not available yet.</p>

  <div class="detail-gallery" data-detail-gallery>Photo gallery</div>

  <dl class="facts-grid" data-detail-facts></dl>
  <p data-detail-voucher style="display:none"></p>

  <div data-detail-movein></div>

  <div data-detail-apply></div>
  <p>Showings are in person after a successful pre-screening (free).</p>

  {# Rental requirements — the ruled site-wide facts (BFP Process Info
     for Tenants, as carried on How to Apply), printed at the bottom of
     every home's page per Jen's direction 2026-11-25. #}
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="req-h">
    <h2 id="req-h"><button type="button" class="req-toggle" data-disclosure-btn aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="req-body">Rental requirements</button></h2>
    <div id="req-body" data-disclosure-panel hidden>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>A state ID is required for the pre-screen</li>
      <li>Income at least 3× the monthly rent — or 1.5× the monthly rent with a Housing Choice Voucher</li>
      <li>Positive references from previous landlords — no past-due amounts owed, no damages, no significant lease violations</li>
      <li>No prior evictions (within 5 years)</li>
      <li>Background check on every application; criminal history is reviewed individually</li>
      <li>No outstanding collections to utility companies</li>
      <li>Mostly positive pay history on the credit report for the last 1 to 2 years. We have no minimum credit score; however, scores under 550 require a double deposit of two months rent.</li>
      <li>No smoking inside the home, of any substance including marijuana</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Costs and deposit</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Application: free. Screening: free.</li>
      <li>Credit/background check: $32 per adult — it runs after the showing, when you decide to move forward. It is not an application fee.</li>
      <li>Deposit: one month's rent — with a Housing Choice Voucher, a flat $1,000</li>
      <li>The deposit is paid in two halves — half at signing, half at move-in</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Animals</h3>
    <p>Animals are allowed on a case by case basis, with a $250 animal deposit and $25/month animal rent.</p>
    <h3>Move-in</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Utilities in your name</li>
      <li>An occupancy permit, where your city requires one</li>
      <li>If you do not have a housing voucher and your credit score is below 550, the double deposit described above applies</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The full requirements are on the <a href="{{ '/how-to-apply/' | url }}">How to Apply</a> page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p><a href="{{ '/find-a-home/' | url }}">← Back to all homes</a></p>
</div>
